@4.3 APPSYS.INC.BL -- start politely, leave it as you found it
.
=4.3 APPSYS.INC.BL -- START POLITELY, LEAVE IT AS YOU FOUND IT
.
=DESCRIPTION
.
.  APPSYS.STARTUP
.      IN: --
.      OUT: APPSYS.MODE APPSYS.COLS APPSYS.ROWS APPSYS.COLOUR
.
.  APPSYS.RESTORE
.      IN: those
.      OUT: screen mode and colour put back
.
.  APPSYS.PANEL.SAVE
.      IN: APPSYS.FILE$ .BANK .X .Y .W .H [.DEV]
.      OUT: a file
.
.  APPSYS.PANEL.LOAD
.      IN: APPSYS.FILE$ .BANK
.      OUT: back where it came from
.
.  APPSYS.PANEL.PUT
.      IN: APPSYS.FILE$ .BANK .X .Y
.      OUT: pasted somewhere else
.
:GOSUB APPSYS.STARTUP
:' ... the application, laid out with APPSYS.COLS / APPSYS.ROWS ...
:GOSUB APPSYS.RESTORE : END
.
.Call STARTUP first, before any SCREEN or COLOR of your own -- it records the
.state as it finds it, so anything you change beforehand is what gets
.restored.
.
.Lay out from APPSYS.COLS / APPSYS.ROWS rather than assuming 80x60. The X16
.boots 80x60 but SCREEN 0 is 40x30, and someone who prefers larger text is
.running one.
.
.APPSYS.DEV defaults to 8. The panel routines themselves moved to
.STASHFILE.INC.BL; the panel file is self-describing -- the stash's 4-byte
.header goes in it -- so loading needs nothing but the name.
.
=SEE ALSO
.
>38|4.3 APPSYS.INC.BL -- start politely, leave it as you found it
>73|STASHFILE.INC.BL -- a saved text rectangle, through a file.
